Release 1.8.0.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 10:31:15

Release 1.7.2.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 10:11:26

Fixed. The text of the wiki chapter, the README, the menu entry's comment, the windows' info texts, hints, tooltips and
notes, the Turn off question of Persistent Journal and the messages of the root part and the VRM service's script was
rewritten to the writing standard: short sentences with one fact each, lists for three or more parts and the purpose
first. No labels were renamed. The Turn off question of Persistent Journal now asks its question first and says that you
will be asked for your password. A fact was corrected: the wiki said that every quickfix that changes the board turns
off only what it turned on itself, but Fix GPU Metrics' Turn off sets fix-metrics back to false whoever turned it on.
IOMMU Off's text in the wiki and in its info no longer
names a modded BIOS. It says that the kernel argument switches the IOMMU off when the BIOS leaves it on. Nothing the
app does has changed. No tests changed.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 19:56:43

Release 1.7.1.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 15:13:54

Release 1.7.0.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 13:50:55

Fixed. VRM Sensors offers Turn on again while its service is there and the module is not loaded. After a load that
failed, an updated quickfix could not be applied: Turn on was off, and the old script stayed in
/var/lib/bc250-quickfix/vrm. Turn on copies the source and the script anew and starts the service.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 12:24:43

Release 1.6.0.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 11:51:00

Fixed. MangoHud Config's Revert pill says Revert changes under it, which was Read the file again.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 10:40:50

Added. Every quickfix's window is a card now, core's template (owner, 21-11-2026). The Refresh pill is gone: a round
refresh symbol of the info symbol's size sits at the right end of the title row, and no pill stands in that row. The
boxes and pills are all as wide as the widest, five on a row at most, and the window is as wide as a full row. A
switch has its boxes, Turn on and Turn off on one row. A switch with four boxes has Turn on and Turn off on a second
row. MangoHud Config has its boxes, Revert and Save on the first row and the FPS log's pills on the second, and its
Delete old logs pill is Delete logs. Tools is the exception: its group pills stay on the left at their own width, with
each group's tools beside its pill instead of under it.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 09:51:30

Fixed. VRM Sensors' service labels its build as a kernel module (chcon -t modules_object_t) before it loads it, where
SELinux is on. On the board the load failed with "insmod: Permission denied": SELinux lets insmod load only a file with
that label, and a file made in /var/lib/bc250-quickfix/vrm has the folder's label.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 00:56:48

Release 1.5.0.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 00:38:50

Added. A quickfix VRM Sensors (bc250-quickfix vrm; owner, 21-11-2026: a Quickfix item beside Sensors Module). It builds
the bc250_vrm kernel module for the running kernel and loads it, now and at every boot, through a service of its own
(bc250-quickfix-vrm.service); a new kernel gets its own build at its first boot. The module's source comes with the
app, unchanged, from Hexxeh/bc250-vrm-dkms v1.1.0 (GPL-2.0), with a Kbuild of our own: upstream's Makefile names
clang, and Bazzite's kernel is built with gcc. Turn off unloads the module and removes the service and its folder,
/var/lib/bc250-quickfix/vrm.

